abase until the beta confirms them. Quest text © Blizzard Entertainment.","narrative":{"details":"One part of undeath no one mentions is what happens when we are injured. How does the skin of an undead heal itself?\n\nWell, it doesn't.\n\nOurs is a cursed life, adventurer. We must take from the living to further our own existence.\n\nWhen we sustain an injury, we must replace our skin which usually means animal hides. Since different hide thicknesses are better for different places on our bodies a variety is key!\n\nBring me wing membranes of a duskbat, hides from a darkhound and skin of a Vile Fin murloc.","objectives":"Bring Shelene Rhobart 8 Duskbat Wing Membranes, 6 Darkhound Hides and 3 Vile Fin Murloc Skin.","offerRewardText":"Ah, excellent! Thank you for acquiring these. I can promise they will be put to good use.","requestItemsText":"Have you gathered the skin I inquired about? Our stocks are running low.It may seem odd to ask for murloc skin but it works well for internal membranes, or surfaces like cheeks or mouths.Similarly, the duskbat wing membranes are especially suited for more delicate areas, like faces or fingers. It prevents the skin from being too... thick.","endText":null,"objectiveText":[]},"narrativeSource":"foreverchanges","prevQuest":null,"nextQuest":null,"nextQuestInChain":null,"giverName":"Shelene Rhobart","turnInName":"Shelene Rhobart","startItemText":null,"startNpcs":[{"name":"Shelene Rhobart","zone":"Tirisfal Glades","x":65.4,"y":60}],"endNpcs":[{"name":"Shelene Rhobart","zone":"Tirisfal Glades","x":65.4,"y":60}],"reputation":[{"faction":"Undercity","factionId":68,"amount":75}],"mentionedItems":[{"name":"Duskbat Wing Membrane","slot":null,"type":"Quest","itemClass":12,"itemId":278242,"icon":"inv_icon_wing07a","quality":1,"itemLevel":1,"requiredLevel":0,"tooltip":["Quest Item","\tQuest"],"tooltipSynthesized":false,"classicTooltip":null,"status":"new","dropChance":null,"dropChanceUnder":false,"unknown":false,"source":"foreverchanges"},{"na